{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/_mcp_models.py` (558 LOC, 33 public pydantic models) hand-mirrors `src/rebar/schemas/*.json`; `src/rebar/schemas/check_mcp_models.py` (174 LOC) plus two drift test modules police the copy. Bug lowly-lawrencium-ovenbird (3a02-66ea-9229-470c) found 41 canonical properties drifted out of the mirror despite the oracle, and model defaults put schema-violating nulls on the wire. The MCP SDK validates every structured result against the advertised `outputSchema` at call time (`mcp/server/lowlevel/server.py`, `jsonschema.validate` in `call_tool`), so the mirror is a second contract that can only be wrong. Decision: advertise the canonical JSON Schema files directly, return the library payload unchanged, delete the mirror and its oracle. Cites are on origin/main 2e28d817a7e (the first comment's audit was on 083620b0; its corrections are in the latest comment).\n\n## Approach\nNew `src/rebar/_mcp_schema.py` (about 220 LOC): `OUTPUT_SCHEMAS_BY_TOOL: dict[str, tuple[tuple[str, ...], Literal[\"object\",\"array\",\"list_of\"]]]`. `object` = the one canonical object schema; `array` = the canonical array schema under `{\"result\": …}` (`get_file_impact`, `get_verify_commands`, `summary`); `list_of` = `{\"result\": {\"type\":\"array\",\"items\": S}}` where S is the named schema, or `{\"anyOf\": [...]}` when two are named: `list_tickets`, `recent_session_logs` (`ticket_state`), `search` (`search_result`), `ready_tickets` (`ready_ticket_summary`, `ticket_state`: lean rows by default, full rows with `full=true`). `inline_schema(names, kind)` hoists `common.schema.json#/$defs/*` into local `$defs` and drops `$schema`/`$id` (mandatory: `jsonschema.validate` cannot resolve cross-file refs). `install_canonical_output_schemas(mcp)` rebinds `mcp.tool` like `_mcp_errors.install_error_guard` (`_mcp_errors.py:77-133`) and, after `original_decorator(fn)` registers, sets `mcp._tool_manager.get_tool(name).fn_metadata.output_schema`, asserting `output_model is not None` and `wrap_output == (kind != \"object\")` so a mis-declared kind fails at startup. `tool_annotation_presets()` moves here verbatim from `_mcp_models.py:524-558`. Install it in `mcp_server.py` after `install_js_safe_guard` (`:608-609`).\nTool bodies return the library dict or list unchanged, annotated `-> dict[str, Any]` / `-> list[dict[str, Any]]` (FastMCP gives the former a pass-through `RootModel` and wraps the latter as `{\"result\": [...]}`; verified by prototype). `_ack`/`_with_push` (`_mcp_writes.py:85-110`) build dicts and omit `None`-valued keys; `show_ticket` adds `plan_review_health` and `cross_session_warning` only when computed; `set_file_impact`/`set_verify_commands` take `list[FileImpactEntry]` / `list[VerifyCommandEntry]` from `rebar.types`, which removes `ctx.dump`/`_dump` (`mcp_server.py:413-419,598`). `transition_ticket`/`reopen_ticket` gain the `transition_result` schema; the other 11 schema-less tools stay schema-less because the LLM ops return `_structured_llm_failure` dicts (`_mcp_llm.py:20-37`) a validator would turn into generic errors. Null-vs-absent rule: emit exactly what the library returns; a key the library omits is absent, never null (as `_OmitUnsetOut`, `_mcp_models.py:35-50`, already does for 15 properties).\nSchema amendments and four new schema files are itemised in the first comment; regenerate `src/rebar/types.py` (`python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types`); wire the new files into `OUTPUT_SCHEMAS` under keys `attach_commits`, `gate_status`, `verify_completion_status`, `write_ack` (precedent: `review_code_gate`). Also: delete the `deprecated` key from every `MCP_ENV_VARS` entry and the `(deprecated alias)` suffix (`mcp_server.py:684`; `scripts/check_server_manifest.py` reads name/description only); delete `uvicorn_graceful_seconds` (`_mcp_serving.py:103,121,137-138`) and `DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS` (`_mcp_health.py:51-52`) with their asserts (`tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py:536,834-839`). Update the `_mcp_budget._wire_bytes` docstring (`:96-101`; model defaults no longer enlarge rows), `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py:96` (drop `dump=`) and `:205-212` (model-field wording), then regenerate `docs/mcp-reference.md`.\n\n## Scope\nDelete: `src/rebar/_mcp_models.py`, `src/rebar/schemas/check_mcp_models.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_model_schema_drift_happy.py`, `..._heldout.py`, the CI step `MCP model schema drift gate` (`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:845-850`), the per-file ignore `pyproject.toml:583`. New: `src/rebar/_mcp_schema.py`, four schema files, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_canonical.py`. Edit: `mcp_server.py`, `_mcp_reads.py`, `_mcp_writes.py`, `_mcp_llm.py:16`, `_mcp_budget.py`, `_mcp_serving.py`, `_mcp_health.py`, `schemas/__init__.py`, `schemas/common.schema.json`, six existing schema files, `types.py` (generated), `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py`, `docs/mcp-reference.md` (generated), `docs/output-schemas.md:232-234`, `docs/release-notes.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` (`--update-stale` for the removed `ci_gate`), and the test rewrites in the first comment. Out of scope: deriving tools from signatures (next story), the MCP-only tools' bodies, CLI or library output.\n\n## Testing\n`tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_canonical.py`: `test_every_advertised_output_schema_equals_its_canonical_file` (every tool in `OUTPUT_SCHEMAS_BY_TOOL`: `tool.outputSchema` from `build_server().list_tools()` equals `inline_schema(names, kind)`; for `object` tools `properties`/`required` also equal the file's); `test_output_schemas_are_self_contained` (no `$ref` contains `.json#`); `test_show_ticket_wire_payload_validates_with_absent_optionals` (via `create_connected_server_and_client_session(build_server()._mcp_server)`; `not result.isError`; `schemas.validator(TICKET_STATE).validate(result.structuredContent)`; `last_reopened_at`, `source_id`, `cross_session_warning` absent; `assignee` present and null); `test_ready_tickets_full_and_lean_rows_validate` (both modes pass the lowlevel validator); `test_write_ack_omits_unset_advisories` (`comment_ticket` ack has no `description_warning`/`cross_session_warning` and `push_status == {\"state\": \"ok\"}`); `test_set_file_impact_accepts_typed_entries` (`[{\"path\":\"a.py\"}]` accepted; `reason: null` refused). `python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types --check`, `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py --check`, `scripts/check_server_manifest.py`, `make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `rebar._mcp_models` and `rebar.schemas.check_mcp_models` do not exist; `grep -rn \"_mcp_models\\|check_mcp_models\" src tests scripts docs .github pyproject.toml Makefile` returns only frozen fixture corpora under `tests/fixtures/` and `docs/experiments/`.\n- [ ] Every tool that advertises an `outputSchema` advertises the canonical file content (the diff test).\n- [ ] A `show_ticket` payload over the real session validates against `ticket_state.schema.json` with absent optionals, and no tool result carries a key whose value the library did not emit (the wire tests).\n- [ ] `list_tools()` count is 64 and exactly 11 tools lack an `outputSchema` (`test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py` partition).\n- [ ] `MCP_ENV_VARS` entries have keys `{name, description}` only and `rebar-mcp --help` output is byte-identical to before (`tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py:186` probe).\n- [ ] `check_server_manifest.py`, `gen_types --check`, `gen_mcp_reference.py --check`, `make verify` exit 0.\n- [ ] Non-codebase: `docs/release-notes.md` lists every field that was null and is now absent (text in the second comment, as corrected in the latest comment)."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792380187368837001,"uuid":"c4ef6e15-8b34-43c5-bb9f-11922b4a76cd"}